error[E0325]: `recurse` takes a block and calls itself
 --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:8:3
  |
8 |   recurse { }
  |   ^^^^^^^ methods with blocks are inlined at each call, so they cannot recurse
help: move the recursion into a helper method without a block, or loop instead
  = see `wid explain E0325`

error[E0319]: `each` needs a block
  --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:13:3
   |
13 |   each
   |   ^^^^ it yields Int
help: pass a block
   |   each do |x|
   |     # …
   |   end
   = see `wid explain E0319`

error[E0319]: `plain` does not take a block
  --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:14:12
   |
14 |   plain(1) { puts "x" }
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^ this block is never called
help: methods receive blocks by declaring `&blk: block(…)` and calling `yield`
   = see `wid explain E0319`

error[E0318]: this proc uses `n` from the code around it
  --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:16:31
   |
16 |   f = ->(x: Int) -> Int { x + n }
   |                               ^ procs cannot capture local variables
   = note: a proc is a plain function pointer; it has nowhere to keep `n` alive
help: pass the value as a parameter, use a block (`do |x| … end`) when the callee yields, or store it in a struct the proc receives
   = see `wid explain E0318`

error[E0319]: block parameter `b` receives nothing
  --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:18:14
   |
18 |   each { |a, b| puts a + b }
   |              ^ the method yields 1 value
   = see `wid explain E0319`

error[E0320]: `main` has no block parameter to `yield` to
  --> tests/ui/block_errors.wid:19:3
   |
19 |   yield 2
   |   ^^^^^^^ nothing to yield to
help: `main` takes no block; call a method that takes a block, or loop here instead
